From b65bf3d3eae307295d6351f9df007294520ce1a1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: T0 <dev@local>
Date: Wed, 5 Aug 2026 09:21:08 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] T1: transfer and disposal schema

Domain entities, enums and EF configuration for API 4.10. No repositories,
services or endpoints yet - those are T3 and T5.

Enums:
- TransactionStatus: ERD 0/1/2 kept, PartiallyReceived=3 (Q5) and
  Disposed=4 (Addendum A) appended.
- TransactionItemReceiveStatus: ERD 0/1/2 kept, Disposed=3 appended.
- TransactionOrigin: UserCreated / AutoGeneratedReturn.

Entities (all append-only, no AuditableEntity, no soft delete per ERD 6.5):
- CardTransfer          -> CardsTransferHistory
- CardTransferProduct   -> CardTransferProducts
- CardTransferItem      -> CardTransferItems
- CardDisposal          -> CardDisposals
- CardDisposalItem      -> CardDisposalItems

CardTransfer carries RowVersion and ActionNotes (Q8), Origin and
ParentTransferId (Q5), and BranchRequestId without an FK until 4.9 (Q2).

Every FK out of the aggregate is NoAction except the two child-to-header
ones, which cascade. Source and target both reference Branches, so NoAction
is required to avoid a multiple-cascade-path error as well as being correct.

CardTransferProducts carries a settlement check constraint: received plus
disposed can never exceed transacted.
